From: Folklore port <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0007] cellFs AIO completes asynchronously; cellVdec playback counters

1. cellFsAioRead ran the read and the completion callback inside the submit
   call. Folklore's movie streamer submits, then marks the request outstanding
   under a mutex and waits for the callback to clear it -- a callback that had
   already run -- so the logo movie never got its first 512 KB and the screen
   stayed black. Reads now complete on a worker thread through their own host
   handle, as lv2 does. PS3_FS_AIO_SYNC=1 restores the old behaviour.
2. ppu_guest_call_set_stack(): a host thread that calls guest code gets its own
   guest stack (the default scratch stack is the same address on every host
   thread). sys_ppu_thread_alloc_host_stack() hands one out from the PPU stack
   region under the thread-table lock.
3. cellVdec: playback counters (AUs, BUSY, decoded, taken, empty) at doubling
   intervals; the per-AU DecodeAu line now needs PS3_VDEC_LOG=1.

